[E-TAILREC] Error: `f` is marked @[tailrec], but a recursive call isn't in tail position
   ╭─[ reject/tailrec-lambda.sw:8:45 ]
   │
 8 │   | Succ n => List.length ([1, 2].map (y => f n))
   │                                             ─┬─  
   │                                              ╰─── it's inside a function passed to `List.map`: it runs when `List.map` calls it, not as a turn of this loop
   │ 
   │ Note: a call is in tail position when its result is the function's result, with nothing left to do after it returns; then each call is a turn of a loop, not a new frame
